OPEN - MEASURED AS A FLIP, MAGNITUDE IN FLIGHT. Not a finish-condition gate.

--- c-defects attempt 10, 2026-09-01 ---

D-C18: `GalaxyDirectRunner.prefill_batched` IS NOT REPRODUCIBLE RUN TO RUN ON LLAMA, AND
       THE TEST THAT CAUGHT IT WAS NOT LOOKING FOR THAT.

HOW IT WAS FOUND. The brief's section 4 says that once D-C6's L1 overflow is fixed, "area 2's
real question becomes askable for the first time: do padded rows change an active row's logits
at active batch 16, 31 and 32?" Attempt 8 queued that node on both models - it had ZERO runs
in RESULTS.md on either, because all of Milestone B's attempts died inside
validate_circular_buffer_region before a row's logits could be read. Attempt 10 read the
results:

  QWEN  zp1/zp2/zp3   3 passed x3   590.75 / 730.40 / 508.97 s
  LLAMA zp4           1 failed, 2 passed   1047.37 s   -> active32 FAILED, "active slots [10]
                                                          moved when only the padding rows changed"
        zp5           3 passed             1008.67 s
        zp6           3 passed              820.67 s
  All six logs: clash 0, TT_FATAL/TT_THROW 0, SKIPPED 0, validate_circular_buffer_region 0.

THE ASSERTION MESSAGE IS MISLEADING, AND THE TEST IS DEGENERATE AT active32.

    rows = _distinct_rows(length, active)
    for filler in (rows[0][:1], rows[-1][:1]):
        padded = list(rows) + [list(filler) for _ in range(GALAXY_PHYSICAL_BATCH - active)]

At active == 32, `GALAXY_PHYSICAL_BATCH - active` is 0, so NO filler rows are appended and
`padded` is `list(rows)` in BOTH iterations. The two invocations therefore receive
BYTE-IDENTICAL input. Nothing about padding is under test at that level. What the test
actually asserts there is that `prefill_batched` returns bit-identical logits when called
twice with the same input, in two `GalaxyDirectRunner` contexts in one process.

So the finding is NOT "padded rows contaminate active rows". It is:

  On Llama, concat-32 prefill returned a different result for slot 10 on the second of two
  identical invocations, in 1 of 3 fresh processes. On Qwen the same case passed 3/3.

A case that flips across fresh processes is a defect and not noise - the house rules say so,
and three of Milestone A's four defects presented as intermittent PASSES for exactly this
reason. It is recorded as a defect.

WHAT IS NOT YET KNOWN, and why three more of the same runs would not tell us. The committed
test asserts `torch.equal` and prints nothing, so 51 minutes of silicon bought one failure, two
passes, and no magnitude. A bfloat16-ulp difference and a wrong buffer read produce the same
`torch.equal` verdict.

THE MEASUREMENT, queued as dc18_repeat_active32_r1..r3 and dc18_repeat_active16_c1
(tttv2_dc18_scratch/test_dc18_concat32_repeat_probe.py, DIAGNOSTIC ONLY, never committed):
one model load, FOUR invocations, ALL SIX pairwise comparisons, reporting per-slot max|diff|
and whether the argmax moved. Six comparisons per model load against the committed test's
three per three processes. It separates three things the committed test cannot:
  1. magnitude - one ulp (accumulation order) vs large (a wrong read);
  2. whether invocation 0 is special, which is D-C12's shape ("only the FIRST device call in a
     warm-cache process is correct") and would make D-C18 and D-C12 one defect;
  3. whether the slot is fixed (geometry) or moves (a race).
The active16 arm is the control: it is the level the committed test passes, and four
invocations there says whether that is reproducibility or insufficient sampling.

RELATION TO D-C6. Separate. D-C6's residual is concat-32 vs SEQUENTIAL prefill differing by
5-18 bfloat16 ulps. D-C18 is concat-32 against ITSELF. D-C6 stays DEFERRED on its own
evidence and this neither strengthens nor weakens it.

CONSEQUENCE FOR THE MILESTONE, stated conservatively: none beyond what is already recorded.
Concat-32 is not on Milestone C's critical path (prefill is sequential per row by the
2026-08-28 scope decision) and nothing downstream may be built on concat-32 for Qwen already.
D-C18 adds that concat-32 on LLAMA - whose length sweep passes at all five lengths - has a
reproducibility question against it that the length sweep never asked.

NOTHING WAS RELAXED AND NOTHING WAS XFAILED. zp4 is recorded as a failure.
